B.Ns=new A.eF("humanoid","Humanoid","The default humanoid shape. The first time each situation a character fails a Convince check, they may reroll the check. ",B.iF)
B.Ng=new A.fv("quadrupedal_herding","Herding","You may not climb. Gain +1 Speed. \nTrampling[Reaction] During your turn, Spend your reaction you may move through an enemy who is a smaller size than you, Make an Status Check vs Str, On Success, Deal {Difference in size between the target and you d6}.\nHerd: [Reaction] During a target ally\u2019s turn, Spend your reaction and move up to the target\u2019s speed as long as you end within 6 spaces of the target.")
B.Nl=new A.fv("quadrupedal_pouncing","Pouncing","You may climb. [Reaction]: At the start of an enemy turn, spend your reaction, dash {Half Level} to a free space range 1 of an enemy, make an Attack vs Str, On success  grapple the target and give them {Half Level} d6 Bleed. ")
B.Ne=new A.fv("quadrupedal_springing","Springing","Ignore difficult terrain, You may not climb. [Reaction] start of any turn, spend your reaction and dash {Half Level} spaces. You may target another creature, if you do make a status check vs Str, on success, knock them prone then dash {Half Level} space to a free space. Otherwise dash to a free space adjacent to the target. Allies may make a Dex defense to resist falling prone.")
B.agV=s([B.Ng,B.Nl,B.Ne],t.CT)
B.Nn=new A.eF("Quadrupedal","Quadrupedal","To stand from prone, you must make and Succeed on either a Brute or Finesse, and it also requires the use of all your speed. If an effect would reduce the costs to stand from prone, instead it costs Half Speed to stand.",B.agV)
B.Nq=new A.eF("bodyplan_hexapodal","Hexapodal and Above","Ignore Difficult Terrain. You may not be knocked prone, when you would gain prone instead lose {Vitality d6} health, you may not reduce or resist this damage. Scuttle [Reaction] start of any turn, spend your reaction and dash {Level} to a free space.",B.iF)
B.Nu=new A.eF("bodyplan_bouncing","Bouncing","Your movement is inconsistent and difficult to predict. Your movement doesn't provoke attacks and you may move through other creatures' spaces. At the end of your turn, choose a random direction and dash {1d6 /2} spaces in that direction. This counts as forced movement for colliding with terrain or being thrown into a pit.",B.iF)
B.No=new A.eF("bodyplan_serpent","Serpent","Ignore difficult terrain and reduce your speed by 2. It costs only 1 speed to stand from prone. Climbing and swimming do not cost extra speed. You may move through other creatures' spaces and your movement doesn't provoke attacks. If you are small, reduce your speed by 1 instead.",B.iF)
B.Nr=new A.eF("bodyplan_mermaid","Mermaid","Reduce your speed by 2. Moving through water doesn\u2019t cost extra movement. Gain 3 * Vitality bonus Health and +1/+2 range on Attacks. If you are small, reduce your speed by 1 instead.",B.iF)
B.Nt=new A.eF("bodyplan_winged","Flying","You have -1 speed when not flying. You may start any situation already concentrating on natural flight.\n\nNatural Flight: [Reaction] During your Turn, spend your reaction and begin concentrating on natural flight. While concentrating, you gain 1 bonus speed, you dash instead of moving, and may fly vertically while moving. You must be in a free space on the ground to use abilities, weapon attacks, or at the end of your turn. You may concentrate on this in addition to other effects. Make only 1 concentration check for all the effects.\n\nIf you are knocked prone, you must check your concentration. Standing from prone still requires movement, and you may not fly until you are standing.",B.iF)
B.Nj=new A.fv("vehicle_armored_transport","Armored Transport","You resist damage caused by attacks targeting allies riding you. [Reaction] After an Ally becomes adjacent to you, you may spend your reaction to have them start riding you, and move into your space wherever you choose.")
B.Nc=new A.fv("vehicle_race_tires","Race Tires","Gain +2 speed.")
B.Nf=new A.fv("vehicle_treads","Treads","Ignore difficult terrain. You resist damage from collision, and are not knocked prone when you fail nor do you take damage on a failure.")
B.Ni=new A.fv("vehicle_winch","Winch","Winch [Reaction] During an Allies turn, Move up to {Level} in a line without provoking attacks. You may do this when prone, but you take 1 Str Damage for each space you move.\nHook [Reaction] During an Ally turn, Make a Melee Ability Attack vs Dex targeting one enemy range {1+Half Level}. On success, Deal {Half level d6} Piercing Damage and pull the target up to {Half Level +1} spaces. You may target allies but they take only {1d6} Piercing Damage.")
B.Nd=new A.fv("vehicle_forklift","Forklift","When you succeed on an attack against an adjacent enemy. You may lift the target until the end of your turn. While lifted, the target doesn\u2019t provoke attacks, and remains adjacent whenever you move, dash, or teleport. ")
B.acm=s([B.Nj,B.Nc,B.Nf,B.Ni,B.Nd],t.CT)
B.Np=new A.eF("bodyplan_vehicle","Vehicle","Gain +2 speed. You cannot climb. Forced movement targeting you is halved but damage from being forced into terrain is tripled. When you are knocked prone, you cannot move nor dash, nor can you end the prone effect. Adjacent allies may spend a [Reaction] or [Action] to remove your prone. Adjacent Allies may ride you, as long as at least 1 of their space can fit in your space, and that space doesn\u2019t contain another ally. For every space worth of ally unable to fit, reduce your speed by 1. While riding, players are prone, they may still be targeted for attacks, and they resist all damage and you take an equal amount of damage as they do if you were not also targeted by the attack. To begin riding and to stop riding players must pay the cost to stand from prone. Hexapod allies aren't damaged for becoming prone because of riding, and stop riding by spending 1 movement point.\nCollision: [Reaction] During your turn, you may move through an enemy who is a smaller size than you, Make an Status Check vs Str, On Success, Deal {Difference in size between the target and you d12} Bludgeoning damage to you and the target and the target is knocked prone. On Problems, You are knocked prone and take {1d8} Bludgeoning damage.",B.acm)
B.Nk=new A.fv("parts_universal","Universal"," Any of your allies may be your host, you can use a [Action] to move from your current host to a target ally. When an ally moves within {Half Level} spaces of you, you may spend your [Reaction] to move from your current host to that ally.")
B.Nh=new A.fv("parts_specific","Specific","You can only have a specific character be your host. At the end of your turn and your host turn, you and your host may give each other Shield and Health. During your turn, you may force your host to move up to {Half your speed}, this movement does provoke attacks. Whenever you or your host heals or gains shields you may give some or all of it to the other.")
B.ago=s([B.Nk,B.Nh],t.CT)
B.Nm=new A.eF("bodyplan_parts","Parts","Your body is a part of another character\u2019s body. You are connected to your host and cannot be separated from each other. Effects that move, dash, teleport, slow, or restrain your host also apply to you and vise versa.You may not use movement points. When you take the [run] action, you may force your host to move up to your speed and this movement can provoke attacks. When you take the [Retreat] action, you may force your host to move half your speed without provoking attacks. When your host doesn\u2019t provoke attacks of opportunity, you also avoid attacks of opportunity. For each size you are more than your host, reduce their speed by 1. If you are smaller or larger than your host, you may reposition yourself relative to your host during your turn so that you are within at least 1 of their spaces. When you die, you must run a generic body with no combat features from spawn to a space adjacent to your host to respond in your body. When your host dies, you are stuck attached to their body until your host moves to space adjacent to you and uses an object interaction to pick you up. When you pick this, choose between being Universal, or Specific.",B.ago)
